WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.607
In the healthcare case, classify each variable before choosing the analysis.

00:00:04.607 --> 00:00:07.062
Diagnosis code is a category.

00:00:07.062 --> 00:00:11.177
Pain score has order. Celsius temperature is interval.

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:13.412
Age has a meaningful zero.

00:00:13.412 --> 00:00:16.337
Comorbidity count is created by counting.

00:00:16.337 --> 00:00:19.147
Length of stay measures elapsed time.

00:00:19.147 --> 00:00:24.182
Also choose an appropriate visualization for pain score and length of stay.

00:00:24.182 --> 00:00:30.667
Finally, decide how diagnosis code should be represented without inventing a numerical order.

00:00:30.667 --> 00:00:37.787
Connect this idea to a university analyzing student records, surveys, and learning-platform activity.

00:00:37.787 --> 00:00:43.257
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:43.257 --> 00:00:50.682
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:50.682 --> 00:00:55.932
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:55.932 --> 00:01:01.873
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
